# Deployment headers for Cloudflare Pages
#
# Cloudflare Pages does not set these by default, and the testbed needs them:
#
#   Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy + Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy  →  cross-origin isolation
#
# ONNX Runtime Web's threaded WASM build requires a cross-origin isolated context to use
# SharedArrayBuffer. Without isolation the runtime still loads the module but fails when it
# tries to construct the session, so the Slow Gate degrades to the mock and the adaptive
# condition stops exercising the learned head — in the deployed origin only, while working
# perfectly on the local dev server, because `vite.config.ts` sets these same headers itself.
# That asymmetry is exactly the kind of failure this milestone must not ship.
#
# `require-corp` (rather than `credentialless`) is used deliberately: every asset the page
# loads — the ONNX graphs and the ORT WASM binary — is served same-origin from this deployment.

/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin

# The ONNX graphs and the compiled WASM payloads are content-addressed by filename only when
# Vite hashes them. Immutable caching is applied to the hashed asset directory, not to the
# model files, because a model swap keeps the same path and must not be served from cache.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Model files may be replaced between deployments for the same path, so they are revalidated.
/models/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
